cpufreq: dt-platdev: create the device at late_initcall_sync

On the Panther X2 (rk3566) cpufreq-dt never probed even with the allowlist
entry (patch 332) and a working cpu-supply regulator (patch 333):

  /sys/kernel/debug/devices_deferred always contains "cpufreq-dt"
  /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/opp/ does not exist
  dmesg has no cpufreq/OPP line at all (the deferred path is dev_dbg())

Reason: cpufreq_dt_platdev_init is a device_initcall(), the same level as
the i2c_add_driver() of the PMIC (fan53555 -> tcs4525) that provides
cpu-supply.  In that order the platform device is probed before the i2c
client exists, so regulator_get_optional() returns -EPROBE_DEFER.  Deferred
probes are only retried when a driver registers, and the PMIC driver has
already registed by then; the regulator appearing later (when the i2c
controller probes its children) does not re-trigger the retry.  The device
therefore stays deferred forever and armclk is pinned at the boot frequency.

Create the platform device from late_initcall_sync() instead: by then
of_platform population, i2c controller, i2c clients and the PMIC regulator
are all in place, so the first probe succeeds.  cpufreq is wanted for
userspace only, so running it after the late initcalls is harmless.

Verified on the board: devices_deferred no longer lists cpufreq-dt,
cpu0/opp/ appears, and scaling_available_frequencies reports
408000..1800000.

--- a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c
@@ -184,4 +184,13 @@
 			       -1, data,
 			       sizeof(struct cpufreq_dt_platform_data)));
 }
-device_initcall(cpufreq_dt_platdev_init);
+/*
+ * Create the platform device late: probe needs both the CPU clock and the
+ * cpu-supply regulator.  With device_initcall() the probe runs before the
+ * i2c PMIC driver has created its regulator, returns -EPROBE_DEFER, and is
+ * never retried -- deferred-probe retries are only triggered by
+ * driver_register(), and by then that driver is already registered.  The
+ * regulator appearing later does not re-trigger the retry, so cpufreq-dt
+ * stays deferred forever.
+ */
+late_initcall_sync(cpufreq_dt_platdev_init);
